hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8086","8133 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Yazid bin Kaysan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Today I will hand over the flag to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God loves.” And his Messenger, so the people became angry, and he said: Where is Ali? They said: He has a problem with his eyes. He said: Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spat on his palms and wiped them. The eyes of Ali were upon him, and the standard was given to him, and God granted victory at his hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8087","8134 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on the Day of Khaybar: “I will give this banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him, and God will grant him victory.” Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I did not like the emirate, until that day, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Ibn Abi Talib and gave him And he said: Walk, and do not turn around until God grants victory to you. So Ali walked, then he stopped, meaning he shouted, O Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said: Why should I fight people? He said: Fight them until they bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God. If they do that, they are forbidden. From me is their blood and their property, except as it is due, and their reckoning is with God.”"
"8088","8135 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, who will conquer him.” Omar said: “I have never liked the leadership, except On that day, he said: So drink for her, so he called Ali and sent him away, then he said: Go and fight until God grants victory to you, and do not turn around. He said: So he walked as long as God wished, then he stopped, and did not turn around, and said: Why should I fight people? He said: Fight them until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Messenger of God, so if they do that, then their blood and their property will be spared, except by right, and their reckoning is with God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8089","8136 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Suhail bin told us Abu Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of Khaybar: “I will hand over the flag to a man.” God and His Messenger love him, and God will grant him victory. Omar said: I had never loved leadership before that day, so he handed it over to Ali, and he said: Fight, and do not turn around. So he walked closer and said: O Messenger of God, why should I fight people? He said: On the condition that they bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Messenger of God, so if they do so, then their blood and their property are protected from me, except as they are due, and their reckoning is with God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8090","8137 Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will give the standard to a man.” He loves God and His Messenger, or he said: God and His Messenger love him. So he called Ali while he was gray-haired, and God opened his hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8091","8138 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: An-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra Bin Yarim said: “Al-Hasan bin Ali came out to us, wearing a black turban, and said: Yesterday there was among you a man whom the ancients had not preceded. Others do not catch up with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God loves him. And His Messenger, so Gabriel fought on his right, and Mikael on his left, and then do not return, meaning his sight, until God grants victory over him. He did not leave a dinar. Not a dirham, except seven hundred dirhams that he took from his own gifts, with which he wanted to buy a servant for his family.”"
"8092","8139 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: 63 He is Abu Awanah, Al-Waddah told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Amr bin Maymun told us, he said: “I was sitting with Ibn Abbas when nine men came to him, and they said: Either You stay with us, or you leave us alone, oh these people. And he was healthy on that day, before he became blind. He said: I am staying with you, so talk, but do not I know what they said: Then he came, shaking off his garment, and said: F and F, they fall upon a man who has ten, and they fall upon a man. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: I will send a man who loves God and His Messenger, whom God will never disgrace. So he looked up and said: Where is Ali in the city? He grinds, and none of you would grind, so he called him, and he was gray-haired and could hardly see, so he blew on his eyes, then he shook the flag three times. So he gave it to him, and he brought Safiyya bint Huyay, and he sent Abu Bakr with the Surah of Repentance, and he sent Ali to succeed him, and he took it from him. He said: No one will go with it, except a man who is from me and I from him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for Al-Hasan, Al-Hussein, and Ali. And Fatima, so he spread a garment over them and said: O God, these are my family, so remove from them the impurity and purify them with a thorough purification. He was the first to He was safer than people after Khadija, and he wore the robe of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he slept, and the polytheists started shooting as they shot the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and they thought that he was the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Abu Bakr came and said: O Prophet of God, and Ali said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Nah and Bir Maimun, so he followed him and entered with him the cave, and the polytheists were shooting at Ali until In the morning, he went out with the people on the campaign against Tabuk, and Ali said: Should I go out with you? He said: No, so he cried and said: Are you not satisfied with being with me? In the same position as Aaron was to Moses, except that you are not a prophet. Then he said: You are my successor, meaning every believer after me. He said: And he closed the doors. The mosque is not the door of Ali, so he used to enter the mosque while he was on the side, and he was on his way and had no other way, and he said: Whose guardian am I? Ali is his guardian. Ibn Abbas said: God told us in the Qur’an that He was pleased with the people of the tree. Has he yet told us that He was displeased? On them? He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Omar when he said: Give me permission to behead him, meaning Hatib, and he said: How do you know, perhaps? God looked at the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8093","8140 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Asadi told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is it not I teach you words that if you say them, you will be forgiven, even though you will be forgiven: There is no god but He, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, there is no god but He, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the Noble Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8094","8141 Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Khaled told us, and he is Ibn Mukhlid, he said: Ali told us, and he is Ibn Salih. Bin Hayy, brother of Hussein bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ali, should I not teach you words that if you say them, God will forgive you, even though He will forgive you?” You say: No. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. There is no god but He, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Heavens, and Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord \the two worlds\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8095","8142 Safwan bin Amr told us, he said: Ahmad bin Khaled told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The words of relief: There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing.” The Generous, Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the Great Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,” Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us He said: Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, similar to it, meaning similar to the hadith of Khaled. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8096","8143 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you words that if you say them you will be forgiven?” Indeed, you will be forgiven: There is no god but God, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Mighty Throne, praise be to God, Lord \the two worlds\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8097","8144 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, On the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you a supplication that if you pray with it, you will be forgiven, and if you are forgiven, I said: Yes, He said: There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, there is no god but Allah, Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne,” Abu Abdul Rahman: Abu Ishaq did not hear from Al-Harith, except four hadiths, of which this is not one of them. We only took him out for disobeying Al-Hussein. Bin Waqid is for Israel, and for Ali bin Salih, and Al-Harith Al-A'war is not like that in the hadith, and Asim and Damra are better than him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8098","8145 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Ali, said: “Some people from Quraysh came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Muhammad, your neighbors and your allies, and some people from... Our servants have come to you with no desire for religion, nor any desire for jurisprudence. Rather, they fled from our lands and our wealth, so return them to us. He said to Abu Bakr: What do you say? He said: They are right, they are your neighbors and your allies. The face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed. Then he said: Perhaps Ali: What do you say? He said: They are right, they are your neighbors and your allies. Then the face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed, then he said: O people. Quraysh, by God, God will send against you a man from among you whose heart God has tested for faith, and he will strike you for religion, or he will strike you. Some of you, so Abu Bakr said: Is it, O Messenger of God? He said: No. Omar said: Is it, O Messenger of God? He said: No, but that is the one He would cut his sandals, and he used to give Ali his own sandals for him to cut.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8099","8146 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Amr bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, On the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen, and I was a young man, and I said: O Messenger of God, you are You sent me to a people among whom there were young people, and I was a young man, and he said: God will guide your heart and make your tongue firm, so what? “I doubted a decision between two people.”"
"8100","8147 Ali bin Khashram informed us, he said: Issa informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, he said “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and I said: You are sending me to a people who are older than me, so how should I make up the case for them?” He said: God will guide your heart and make your tongue firm. He said: “I have not experienced government yet.”"
"8101","8148 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari. On the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen to judge among them, so I said: O Messenger of God, I have no knowledge of judgement.” Then he struck his hand on my chest and said: Oh God, guide his heart and guide his tongue. I never doubted a decision between two people until I sat in my seat. “This,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: Tell me who He heard Ali. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Bakhtari did not hear anything from Ali. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8102","8149 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen when I was a young man, so I said: O Messenger of By God, you sent me when I was young to a people with teeth to judge among them, and I had no knowledge of judgment. So he put his hand on my chest, then said: Indeed? God will guide your heart and make your tongue firm, O Ali. When the two adversaries sit before you, do not judge between them until you hear from the other, as you heard from The first is that if you do that, the judgment will become clear to you. Ali said: “There is no problem for me yet in making a judgment.”"
"8103","8150 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha bin Mudarib, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen, and I said: You are sending me to a people who are older than me.” To judge between them, and he said: God will guide your heart and make your tongue firm.” Shayban said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Habashi, on the authority of Ali"
"8104","8151 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Habashi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of God, you are sending me to people with teeth. I fear that I will not be correct. He said: God will strengthen your tongue and guide your heart. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8105","8152 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had broad doors in the mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he said the salutation: “Block these doors, except the door of Ali.” Some people spoke about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and thanked God and praised him. upon him, then he said: “As for what follows, I have been ordered to close these doors except the door of Ali, and your speaker said about it, by God, I have not blocked it, nor I opened it, but I was ordered to do something so I followed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8106","8153 I read about Muhammad bin Sulaiman Luwayn, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ibrahim Bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, and he did not say once, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there were some people with him. Sitting, then Ali entered, and when he entered, they left, and when they came out, they blamed each other, and they said: By God, he did not take us out and bring him in. So they returned, so they entered, and he said: By God, I did not bring it in and take you out, but rather God brought it in and brought you out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8107","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ali bin Qadim told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Al-Harith Ibn Malik, he said: I came to Mecca, and I met Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and I said: Did you listen to Ali, wearing a niqab? He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque, and a call was made to us at night: “Let everyone leave the mosque except the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted him and the family of Ali. He said: So we left, and when the morning came, Omar came to him and said: O Messenger of God, you took out your friends and uncles, and you settled in This boy, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was not commanded to take you out, nor to put this boy in residence. Indeed, God commanded “With it,” Fitr said: On the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Raqim, on the authority of Saad, that Al-Abbas came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: Our doors were closed except the door of Ali. He said: I neither opened it nor closed it. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abdullah bin Sharik is not With that, and Al-Harith bin Malik, I do not know him nor Abdullah bin Al-Raqim, Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abdullah bin told us Omar, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Raqim, on the authority of Saad, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8108","8155 Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Miskin told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Abu Balj is Yahya bin Abi Suleiman. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the doors of the mosque be blocked, and they were blocked.” “Except the door of Ali.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8109","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad told us, he said: al-Waffah told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Amr told us Ibn Maimun, he said: Ibn Abbas said: “He blocked the doors of the mosque except the door of Ali, so he used to enter the mosque while he was on the side, and it is his way not He has a different path.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8110","8157 أَخْبَرَنَا بِشْرُ بْنُ هِلالٍ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنَا جَعْفَرٌ وَهُوَ ابْنُ سُلَيْمَانَ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنَا حَرْبُ بْنُ شَدَّادٍ ، عَنْ قَتَادَةَ ، عَنْ سَعِيدِ Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched the Battle of Tabuk, he left Ali in Medina. They said about him: He was bored and hated his company, so he followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he caught up with him on the road, and he said: O Messenger of God, you left me behind in Medina. With children and women, until they said: He bored him and he hated his company, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ali, I have only left you in charge of my family. Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8111","8158 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: You are to me as Aaron was to Moses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8112","8159 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Musab told us, that Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Safwan Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “Aren’t you satisfied to be with me? “In the position of Aaron to Moses, except for prophecy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8113","8160 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Hashim bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Tabuk, Ali, may God be pleased with him, came out to mourn him, and he cried. He said: O Messenger of God, will you leave me with those who disagree? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Ali, are you not satisfied with being in the same position as me? Aaron from Moses, except for prophecy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8114","8161 Ishaq bin Musa bin Abdullah bin Musa bin Abdullah n Yazid Al Ansari told me, he said: Dawud bin Kathir told us Al-Raqi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You “To me is the status of Aaron to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8115","8162 Safwan bin Amr told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khaled told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah al-Majishun told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab said, Ibrahim ibn Sa`d told me that he heard his father Sa`d saying: The Prophet said, May God bless him and grant him peace to Ali: “Aren’t you satisfied that you are to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophecy?” Sa’id said: I was not satisfied until I went to Saad and said: Something your son told me about you. He said: What is it? And he rebuked me. I said: No, no, for this. He said: What is it, oh? My nephew? So I said: Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say such-and-such to Ali? He said: Yes, and he pointed to his ears. Otherwise, they would remain silent. I heard him say that.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yusuf ibn al-Majshun disagreed with him, and he narrated it on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa`id. On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, and he continued his narration, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, Ali bin Zaid bin Judaan (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8116","8163 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Al-Shawareb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are to me as Aaron was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me. Sa’id said: So I would have loved to tell Sa’d about that, so I went to him and said: What hadith did he tell me about you? Amer, then he put his two fingers in his ears and said: I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, otherwise they will remain silent.” He narrated this hadith Shu`bah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, but he did not mention Amer bin Saad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8117","8164 Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Miskin told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrates, on the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are to me as Aaron was to Moses.” He said, “First Once: I was satisfied, I was satisfied. I asked him after that, and he said: Yes, yes. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know that anyone followed Abd al-Aziz. Ibn Al-Majishun, based on his narration, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyib, other than Ibrahim Ibn Sa’d, on the authority that Ibrahim Ibn Sa’d He narrated this hadith, on the authority of his father (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8118","8165 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Saad narrating, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said to Ali: “Aren’t you satisfied to be of me? “in the position of Aaron to Moses” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8119","8166 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Talha bin Yazid bin Rukana told me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father Saad, that he heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace. He said to Ali when he succeeded him in the Battle of Tabuk against his people: “Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except “There is no prophet after me.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith was narrated, on the authority of Aamir bin Sa’d, on the authority of his father, other than the hadith of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8120","8167 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, he said: Bukayr bin Mismar told us, he said: I heard Amer bin Saad, saying: Muawiyah said to Saad bin Abi Waqqas: “What prevented you from cursing Ali bin Abi Talib?” He said: I will not curse him as long as you mentioned three things. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Because it is mine.” He said, “One is dearer to me than red camels. I do not curse it as I mentioned when it came down.” The revelation was upon him, so he took Ali, his two sons, and Fatima, and put them under his garment, then said: O Lord, these are my family and my household, and do not I insulted him when he succeeded him in a battle he fought. He said: You left me behind with the boys and women. He said: Are you not content to be to me in the same position as Aaron was to me? Moses, except that he had no prophecy, and I do not curse him. I did not mention that on the Day of Khaybar when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will be given this banner. A man who loves God and His Messenger, and God grants victory at his hands. So we talked, and he said: Where is Ali? They said: He is a gray man. He said: Call him, so they called him. So he spat in his eyes, then gave him the standard, and God granted him victory. By God, Muawiyah did not mention him in a word until he left Medina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8121","8168 Zakaria bin Yahya informed us, he said: Abu Musab informed us, on the authority of Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Al-Ja’id, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of her father, “Ali went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he came to Thaniyat al-Wada’, intending to invade Tabuk, and Ali was complaining, saying: Will you leave me behind? The disobedient ones? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except for prophethood? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8122","8169 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, succeeded Ali bin Abi Talib in the Battle of Tabuk, and he said: O Messenger of God, will you leave me in charge of the women and children? He said: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Laith disagreed with him, so he said : On the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8123","8170 Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman informed us, saying: Al-Muttalib informed us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, On the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali in the Battle of Tabuk: “You are to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that he is not a prophet.” After me,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shu’bah is better, and Layth is weak, and the hadith was narrated by Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8124","8171 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Al-Ja’id, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of her father, “Ali went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he came to Thaniyat al-Wada’, intending to invade Tabuk, and Ali was complaining and saying: Will you leave me alone? With those who disagreed? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except for prophethood? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8125","8172 Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, he said: Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the battle of Tabuk, and succeeded Ali. He said to him: Will you leave me behind? He said to him: Are you not satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8126","8173 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Fitr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Raqim Al-Kanani, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: You are to me as Aaron was to Musa,” Israel said: On the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik, on the authority of Saad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8127","8174 Ahmad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ali bin Qadim told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik said: Saad bin Malik said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked on his red she-camel, and left Ali behind. Then Ali came and took hold of the she-camel, and said: “O Messenger of God, the Quraysh claimed that you had only succeeded me, that you had burdened me, and you hated I accompanied me, and he cried for me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out to the people: Is there anyone among you who does not have a mother-in-law? O son of Abi Talib, are you not satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? Ali said: I am satisfied with God. And on the authority of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8128","8175 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning bin Saeed, he said: Musa Al-Juhani told us, he said: I entered upon Fatima’s daughter Ali, and my companion said to her: Do you have anything proven about your father? She said: Asma bint Umays told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are to me what Aaron was to Moses, except “There will be no prophet after me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8129","8176 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Juhani, he said: I met Fatima, the daughter of Ali, and she Eighty years old, so I said to her: Do you keep anything from your father? She said: No, but Asma’ bint Umays told me that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O Ali, you are of mine.” In the same position as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8130","8177 Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Hassan, who is Ibn Salih, told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Juhani, on the authority of Fatima bint Ali, on the authority of Asma bint Umays, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are of mine.” “In the same position as Aaron was to Moses, except that he is not after me.”"
"8131","8178 Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Naysaburi and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, and the wording is for Muhammad, saying: He narrated to us. Amr bin Talha, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Ali “used to say during the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God says: If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels? Who will turn back? By God, we will not turn back. Our successors after God had guided us. By God, if he died or was killed, I would have fought for what he fought for until he died. By God, I am his brother and his guardian. And his heir, and his cousin, and who has more right to it than me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8132","8179 Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah, On the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, “A man said to Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, why did you inherit from your cousin and not your uncle?” He said: Plural The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, or he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called the Banu Abdul-Muttalib and prepared a mud of food for them. He said: Until they were full and the food remained as it was, as if it had never been touched. Then he called for something to be drunk and they drank until they had had enough and the drink remained as it was, as if it had never been touched. Or he did not drink, so he said: O Banu Abdul Muttalib, I have been sent to you in particular, and to people in general, and you have seen from this verse As you have seen, which of you pledged allegiance to me on the condition that he be my brother, my companion, and my heir, but no one stood up to him, so I stood up to him, and I was younger? The people, and he said: Sit, then he said three times, I would stand up to him, and he would say: Sit, until it was the third time that he struck my hand with his hand. Then he said: “Therefore, I inherited from my cousin rather than my uncle.”"
"8133","8180 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Othman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, On the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasira, on the authority of Abu Sulayman Al-Juhani, he said: I heard Ali, on the pulpit, saying: “I am the servant of God, and the brother of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. None would say it except a liar and slanderer. Then a man said: I am the servant of God and the brother of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he was strangled and carried.”"
"8134","Bishr bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Ali is from me, and I am from him, and the guardian of every believer.”"
"8135","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Sharik told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: he told me Habashi ibn Junada al-Saluli said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ali is from me, and I am from him.” So I said to Abu Ishaq: Where did you hear it? He said: Ali stopped here and told me. Israel narrated it, and he said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’"
"8136","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are from me, and I am from you.” It was narrated by Al-Qasim bin Yazid Al-Jarmi, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq. On the authority of Hubayra, Hani, on the authority of Ali"
"8137","8184 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra bin Yarim, And Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali, said: “When we came from Mecca, the daughter of Hamza called: O uncle, O uncle, so Ali took her to her. So he took it and said to Fatima: “Beware of your cousin.” So he carried her and Ali, Ja’far, and Zaid disputed over her, and Ali said, “I have more right to her.” She is my paternal uncle’s daughter. Ja’far said: My paternal uncle’s daughter, and her paternal aunt is below me. Zayd said: My brother’s daughter. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled for her. He greeted her aunt, and said: The aunt is in the same position as the mother, and he said to Ali: You are from me, and I am from you, and he said to Ja`far: You resemble my character. And my morals, and he said to Zaid: O Zaid, you are our brother and our protector."
"8138","8185 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, On the authority of Zaid bin Yatha’, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let the Banu Wali’ah cease, or I will send to them A man like myself, who carries out my command among them, kills the fighter, and takes captive the offspring. The only thing that bothered me was when Omar kept me in custody behind me: Who? He means? So I said: It is not you, nor is your friend. He said: Who does he mean? He said: The one who cuts shoes. He said: And Ali cuts shoes? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8139","8186 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibn Abi Omar and Abu Marwan told us, they said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Nafi’ bin Ujair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for You, O Ali, are pure and secure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8140","8187 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Habashi bin Junada Al-Saluli said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ali is from me, and I am from him, and no one can perform on my behalf except me or Ali.”"
"8141","8188 Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, saying: Affan and Abd al-Samad informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Bara’a with Abu Bakr, then he called him and said: It is not appropriate for anyone to convey this except a man of My family, so he called Ali and gave it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8142","8189 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad informed us, saying: Abu Nuh, whose name is Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan Qarad, told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Yatha’, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent innocently to the people of Mecca with Abu Bakr, then Ali followed him and said to him: Take the letter and take it to the people of Mecca. He said: So I followed him and took the letter from him. So Abu Bakr left, looking depressed, and said: O Messenger of God, was something revealed about me? He said: No, I have been ordered to inform him, or a man from my household. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8143","8190 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told us, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ruqaym, on the authority of Saad, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Bakr to exonerate him, even if he was Somehow, he sent Ali and took it from him, then he walked with it, and he found Abu Bakr himself, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “No one can perform on my behalf except me, or a man from me.”"
"8144","8191 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I read to Abu Qarrah Musa bin Tariq, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Abdullah bin told me Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from the Umrah al-Ji’ranah, he sent Abu Bakr On the Hajj, so we went with him until we were on the verge of limping. He dressed in the morning, then he sat up to say “Allahu Akbar,” and he heard foaming behind his back. Then he stopped saying “Allahu Akbar” and said: “This is the foam of the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It appeared to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Hajj, perhaps it will be the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we will pray with him. Then, lo, Ali is performing it, and Abu Bakr said to him: Amir or A messenger? He said: No, but a messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with a statement to read it to the people at the Hajj sites, so we came to Mecca. The day before the tarwiyah, Abu Bakr stood up and addressed the people, telling them about their rituals, until when he finished, Ali stood up and recited. The people owed a patent until he sealed it, then we went out with him until the day of Arafat came. Abu Bakr got up and addressed the people, telling them about Their rites, until when they were finished, Ali got up and recited to the people Surat Al-Baraa until he concluded it. Then it was the Day of Sacrifice, so we dispersed, so when he returned Abu Bakr addressed the people, telling them about their sacrifice, about their sacrifice, and about their rituals. When he finished, Ali got up and recited to the people: He was acquitted until he sealed it. When it was the first day of the army, Abu Bakr got up and addressed the people. He told them how to march, and how to shoot. So he taught them their rites, and when he finished, Ali got up and read to the people: The Innocence until he sealed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8145","8192 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: he told us Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage And the stream of Khumm descended. He ordered groups of people to get up, then he said: It is as if I had been called, so I responded. Indeed, I have left among you two burdens, one of them greater than The other: The Book of God, and my family, my family, so see how you succeed me in them, for they will not separate until they return to me at the Fountain, then he said: Indeed, God is my master, and I am the guardian of every believer. Then he took Ali’s hand and said: Whoever I was his guardian, this is his guardian. Oh God, be the guardian of whomever is his guardian. And whoever had been hostile to him returned, so I said to Zaid: Did I hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: There was no one in the outbreaks who did not see him with his own eyes. And he heard it with his own ears.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8146","8193 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, On the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us with a secret group, and he appointed Ali to help us. When we returned, he asked us: How did you see? The company of your friend? Either I complained about him, or someone else complained about him. So I raised my head and was a proud man, and behold, the face of the Messenger of God appeared. He turned red and said: Whoever I am a guardian of, Ali is his guardian. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8147","8194 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniya told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Buraydah told me, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with Ali to Yemen, and I saw He became agitated, so when I returned his complaint to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he raised his head to me and said: O Buraida, whose master was I? “Ali is his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8148","8195 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Abd al-Malik Ibn Abi Ghaniyeh told us, he said: Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Buraydah, he said: “I went out with Ali to Yemen, and I saw a faintness from him, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I mentioned Ali, so I looked at him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his face change and said: O Buraida, aren’t you Who has more right to the believers than they themselves? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8149","8196 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Abdul Wahid Ibn Ayman, on the authority of his father, that Saad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.”"
"8150","8197 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, Ibn Abi Adi informed us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Maymun Abi Abdullah, Zaid bin Arqam said: “He rose The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thanked God and praised Him, then said: Do you not know that I have more right over every believer than himself? They said: Yes, we bear witness that you are more worthy of every believer than himself. He said: For whomever I am his master, this is his master. He took the hand. \Ali\"""""
"8151","8198 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi and Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi informed us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Musa, he said: Hani bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Talha Al-Ayami, he said: Umairah bin Saad told us, that he heard Ali reciting in Al-Rahba: Whoever heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master.” Then a few dozen people stood up and bore witness. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8152","8199 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Sa’id bin Wahb, He said: Five or six of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and testified that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who were you?” His master, Ali is his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8153","8200 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Khalaf told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Sa`id bin told me Wahb, six of those next to him stood up, and Zaid bin Yatha’ said: Six of those next to me stood up, and they testified that they had heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8154","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Imran bin Aban told us, he said: Sharik told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Yatha’, He said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib saying on the pulpit of Kufa: “I am a man seeking God, and I seek no one except the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Whoever heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whomever befriends him and is hostile to him. Whoever was hostile to him, then six stood up from one side of the pulpit, and six from the other side, and testified that they had heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Saying that, Sharik said: So I said to Abu Ishaq: Did you hear Al-Baraa bin Aazib narrating this on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8155","8202 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ja’far, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, narrated to me, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Imran. Ibn Husayn, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army and appointed Ali Ibn Abi Talib as an authority over them, so he went on in secret, and was wounded. Then they disapproved of him, and they joined forces with four of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when we met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We informed him of what he had done, and when the Muslims returned from a journey, they would start with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and greet him, then They departed to their journey, and when the company arrived, they greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then one of the four stood up and said: O Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Have you not seen Ali bin Abi Talib do such-and-such, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned away from him, then he stood up, meaning the second one? He said the same as that, then the third stood up and said the same as what he said, then the fourth stood up and said the same as what they said, so the Messenger of God came to them. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and anger appeared on his face. He said: What do you want from Ali? Ali is from me, and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8156","8204 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali said: I entered upon Umm Salamah and she said: Is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reviled among you? So I said: Glory be to God or God forbid. She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever reviles Ali has reviled me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8157","8205 Abdul-A’la bin Wasil bin Abdul-A’la informed us, saying: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Abi Abdullah, he said: Abu Bakr bin Khalid bin Arafatah told us, he said: I saw Saad bin Malik in Medina, and he said: It was mentioned that you are cursing Ali. I said: We did. He said: Perhaps you caused it? I said: God forbid. He said: “Do not curse him, for if the saw is placed on my side, I will curse Ali as I cursed him after I heard from the Messenger of God.” What I heard, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"8158","8206 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Fitr bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Fitr told us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Aamir bin Wathilah, he said: “Collected Ali of the people in the spacious area, and he said: I adjure by God every person who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on the Day of Ghadir Khumm what he heard, so he stood up. People testified that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Do you not know that I have more right to the believers than to themselves? And he was standing, then he took Ali’s hand and said: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. Oh God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him, he said. Abu Al-Tufayl: So I went out with something in my mind about it, and I met Zaid bin Arqam, and I told him, and he said: Do you not deny that I heard it from the Messenger of God? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” and the pronunciation is by Abu Dawud. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8159","8207 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Ibrahim told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Musa bin Yaqoub told me, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Mismar, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, and Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He addressed the people and said: As for what follows, O people, I am your guardian. They said: You have spoken the truth. Then he took Ali’s hand and raised it, then He said: This is my guardian and the one who will deliver on my behalf, and to God is whoever is loyal to him, and whoever is hostile to him is hostile to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8160","8208 Ahmad bin Uthman Abu Al-Jawza told us, he said: Ibn Uthma told us, he said: Musa bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Mismar, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Ali’s hand, delivered a speech, thanked God and praised him.” Then he said: Do you not know that I have more right over you than yourselves? They said: Yes, you are right, O Messenger of God. Then he took Ali’s hand. So he raised it and said: Whoever I am a guardian of, this is his guardian, for God is loyal to whoever is loyal to him, and is hostile to whoever antagonizes him."
"8161","8209 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Ja’far bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Muhajir bin Mismar, who said: Aisha bint Saad told me, on the authority of Saad, who said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the road to Mecca. And he was directed to her. When he reached Ghadir Khumm, the people stopped, then those who went on turned away, and those who stayed behind followed him. When the people gathered towards him, he said: O The people: Have I conveyed the message? They said: Yes. He said: O God, bear witness. He said it three times. Then he said: O people: Who is your guardian? They said: God and His Messenger. Three times, then he took Ali’s hand and made him stand up, then he said: Whoever Allah and His Messenger are his guardian, this is his guardian. \He was hostile to him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8162","8210 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Abdul Jalil bin Atiya told us, he said: he told us Abdullah bin Buraidah, he said: My father told me, he said: “None of the people was more hateful to me than Ali bin Abi Talib, until I loved him.” A man from Quraysh, whom I do not love except because of Ali’s hatred. So that man was sent on a horse, and I accompanied him, and I did not accompany him except because of Ali’s hatred. He was taken captive, so he wrote to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to send him someone to take his fifth to him. So he sent Ali to us, and while he was captive, he was a female servant. He bestowed the captivity, so when five days of captivity, the slave woman became one of the five, then five, so she became among the family of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then five, So it became among the family of Ali, so he came to us and his head was dripping, so we said: What is this? He said: Did you not see the maid of honor became among the fifth, then she became among the five? The family of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then it came to the family of Ali, so I signed on to it. He wrote and sent me confirming his letter to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, confirming what Ali said, so I started saying to him, and he says: He spoke the truth, and I say, and he says: He spoke the truth, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand. And he said: Do you hate me? I said: Yes. He said: Do not hate him, but if you love him, love him even more. By the One in whose hand is my soul. “The Ali family’s share of the fifth is better than that of a maid of honor. There was no one after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was more beloved to me than Ali,” Abdul said. Allah bin Buraidah: By Allah, there is no one in the hadith between me and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except my father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8163","8211 Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahb, he said: Ali said in Al-Rahba: “I adjure by God the one who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Ghadir Khumm, saying: ‘Indeed, God is the Guardian of the believers. And whoever I am his guardian, then this is his guardian. Oh God, befriend whoever befriends him, antagonize whoever antagonizes him, and support whoever supports him. He said: Then Sa`id said: He rose to There were six beside me, and Zaid bin Yatha’ said: Six stood with me, and Amr Dhu Murr said: Love whoever loves him, and hate whoever hates him. The hadith, narrated by Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Amr Dhul Murr: He loved"
"8164","8212 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Khalaf told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr Dhi Bitter, he said: “I witnessed Ali, with ar-Rahba, the Companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, chanting: Which of you heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: On the day of Ghadir Khumm, what did he say? Then some people stood up and testified that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever I am the master of, then Ali is Ali.” “His Master, O God, befriend whoever befriends him, be hostile to whoever is hostile to him, love whoever loves him, hate whoever hates him, and support whoever supports him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8165","8213 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Ali, He said: “By the One who split the grain and created the breath at the time of the unlettered Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, no one will love me except a believer, and no one will hate me except a believer.” \hypocritical\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8166","8214 Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Ali He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrusted me: “No one will love me except a believer, and no one will hate me except a hypocrite.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8167","8215 Yusuf bin Issa informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, he said: Al-A’mash informed us, on the authority of Adi, on the authority of Zirr, he said: Ali said: “ It is the covenant of the unlettered Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to me: “No one will love you except a believer, and no one will hate you except a hypocrite.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8168","8216 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, saying: Yahya bin Ma’in told us, he said: Abu Hafs Al-Abar told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasira, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O Ali, in you is a parable of Jesus. The Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they put him down.” In the house that does not exist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8169","8217 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Ala’, he said: A man asked Ibn Omar, on the authority of Othman, said: “He was one of those who turned away on the day the two armies met, so God turned to him in repentance, then he committed a sin and they killed him, and asked him about Ali, so he said: Do not ask about him, do you not see his status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
"8170","8218 Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Arar, He said: I asked Abdullah bin Omar, I said: Don’t you tell me about Ali and Othman? He said: “As for Ali, this is his house, out of the love of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I will not tell you about anything else. As for Uthman, he On the day of Uhud he committed a major sin, so God pardoned him, and he committed a minor sin against you, so you killed him.”"
"8171","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Arar, he said: I asked Ibn Umar while he was in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Ali and Uthman. He said: “As for Ali, do not ask me about him. And look at his place from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. There is no house in the mosque other than his own, and as for Uthman, he committed a sin. Great was the day the two groups met, and God pardoned him and forgave him, and he committed a lesser sin against you, and you killed him.”"
"8172","8220 Ismail bin Yaqoub bin Ismail told us, he said: Ibn Musa told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah said: A man came to Ibn Omar and asked him about Ali. He said: “Do not ask about Ali, but look at his house from the houses of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I hate him.” He said: “May God hate you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8173","8221 Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: He asked Abd al-Rahman Qutham ibn al-Abbas: “From where did Ali, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inherit? He said: Indeed, we were more courteous of him and were harsher.” It is necessary for him. Zayd bin Abi Anisa succeeded him, and he said: On the authority of Khalid bin Qutham."
"8174","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Qutham, it was said to him: “Why did Ali inherit the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rather than your grandfather, who was his paternal uncle?” He said: “Ali was the first to give us priority over him.” \And We encouraged him firmly.\"""""
"8175","8223 Abdah bin Abdul Rahim informed me, he said: Amr bin Muhammad informed us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: Abu Bakr asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to call for permission, and he heard Aisha’s loud voice. And she said: “By God, I know that Ali is more beloved to you than my father.” So Abu Bakr leaned towards her to slap her, and said: O daughter of so-and-so. I see you raising your voice against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seized him, and Abu Bakr left. Angry, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Aisha, how did you see me saving you from the man? Then Abu Bakr asked for permission That is, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Aisha reconciled, and he said: Bring me into peace just as you brought me into war, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: We have done it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8176","8224 Muhammad bin Adam told me, he said: Ibn Abi Ghaniyeh told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of all of us, and he is Ibn Umair. He said: I went in with my mother to see Aisha, and I was a boy, so I mentioned Ali to her, and she said: I have never seen a man more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And there is no woman more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than his wife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8177","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin al-Khattab told us, trustworthy, he said: Muhammad bin Ismail bin Raja al-Zubaidi told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Juma’ bin Umair, he said: I entered with my mother to see Aisha, and I heard her asking her from behind the veil, On the authority of Ali, she said: “You are asking me about a man. I do not know anyone who was more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than him, and I do not know anyone more beloved to him than him. \His wife\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8178","8226 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, he said: Shadhan told us, on the authority of Ja’far al-Ahmar, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, said: “A man came to my father and asked him: Which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Who are the women? He said: The most beloved of the people to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among the women was Fatima, and among the men: Ali,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: Abdullah bin Ata is not strong in hadith."
"8179","8227 Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, and he is Ibn Abu Unaysa, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, he heard Ali saying: “I was entering The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if he was praying, he said the Subhanahu, so I entered, and if he was not praying, he gave me permission, so I entered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8180","8228 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid and Abu Kamil told us, they said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Amara bin Al-Qaqa’ told us, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, he said: He said: Ali: “It was an hour in the early dawn when I would enter upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and while he was praying he said the Sublime, and that was his permission for me.” And if he is not praying, give me permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8181","8229 Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr, he said: He told us Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, said: “I had from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, an hour of dawn during which I would come to him. I asked for permission, and if I found him praying, he said the Subhanahu, so I entered, but if I found him empty, he gave me permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8182","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told me, he said: Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Ibn Naji, he said: Ali said: “I had two entrances to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: an entrance at night, and an entrance during the day, so when I entered at night, he would clear his throat.” “Lee.” Shurahbil ibn Mudarrak disagreed with him in his chain of transmission and agreed with him in his saying: Tanahah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8183","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Shurahbil, meaning Ibn Mudrak al-Ja’fi, told me, he said: Abdullah bin Naji Al-Hadrami told me, on the authority of his father, who was the companion of Ali’s purification, he said: Ali said: “I had the status of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not for any of the creatures, so I used to come to him every morning and say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet of God. If he cleared his throat “I will go to my family, otherwise I will enter upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8184","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Al-Masawar told me, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Hind Al-Jamali, He said: Ali said: “When I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would give me, and if I remained silent, he would give me something.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8185","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, he said: “When I asked, I would be given, and if I remained silent, I would show.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8186","8234 Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad and another man told us, On the authority of Zazan, they said: Ali said: “By God, when I asked, I was given, and if I remained silent, I began.”"
"8187","8235 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Hakim al-Madaini, he said: Abu Maryam told us, he said: he said Ali: “I set out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until we came to the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, climbed on my shoulders. So Ali got up with him, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw his weakness, he said to him: Sit down, so he sat down, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended. And he said: Climb on my shoulders, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up with him, and Ali said: It makes me imagine that if I wanted I reached the horizon of the sky, so I ascended to the Kaaba, and upon it was a statue made of yellow or copper, and I began to treat it to remove it from the right and from the left, from the front and from the other. In front of him, and behind him, until when I gained control of him, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Throw him, so I threw him, and I broke him. Just as bottles are broken, then I got down, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I set out to race until we hid ourselves in houses for fear that “One of the people will meet us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8188","8236 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of His father, he said: “Abu Bakr and Omar proposed to Fatima, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ‘She is young,’ so he proposed to Ali. So he married her to him.”"
"8189","8237 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Hatim bin Wardan told us, he said: Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani told us, on the authority of Abu Yazid Al-Madani, on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, said: “I was at the wedding of Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the morning came, the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He knocked on the door, and Umm Ayman opened the door for him. He said: O Umm Ayman, call for my brother for me. She said: He is your brother and you may marry him. He said: Yes, Umm Ayman, and the women heard the voice of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they moved away. She said: And I hid in a corner. She said: Then Ali came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and sprinkled water on him, then said: Call Fatima for me. Then a rag of modesty, so he said to her: It may mean that I married you to the most beloved of my family. He prayed for her and sprinkled some water on them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. Peace be upon him. He saw darkness and said: Who is this? I said: Asma’. He said: The daughter of Umays. I said: Yes. He said: I was at the wedding of Fatima’s daughter. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would you honor him? I said: Yes. She said: So he prayed for me. Sa`id bin Abi Orouba disagreed with him, and he narrated it on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8190","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sadran told us, he said: Suhail bin Khallad Al-Abdi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sadran told us Whether, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married May God bless him and grant him peace. He presented Fatima with Ali as a gift with her, a conditional bed, a pillow made of human beings stuffed with fiber, and a skin-skin. He said: And they came. With the sand in the house? And he said to Ali: If you bring it, do not approach it until I come to you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and knocked. The door, so Umm Ayman came out to him, and he said to her: Then my brother? She said: How can he be your brother, since your daughter married him? He said: He is my brother, he said Then he approached her and said to her: Have you come to honor the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: Yes, so he prayed for her and said to her: Good? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and said: The Jews used to take a man away from his wife when he had intercourse with her. He said: So he called The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a basin of water, spit in it, and sought refuge in it. Then he called Ali and sprinkled some of that water on his face. And his chest, and his arms. Then he called Fatima, and she began to stumble in her dress out of shyness before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he did to her. Like that, then he said to her: By God, I would not marry you to the best of my family. Then he got up and left. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8191","8239 Salman bin Ubayd Allah informed us, he said: Bahz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who is Ibn al-Fadl, he said: Abu Nadra narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Saeed, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A rogue woman passes by a group of Muslims, and the leader of the two groups will kill her justly.”"
"8192","8240 Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubai Najih, on the authority of his father, that Muawiyah mentioned Ali bin Abi Talib, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: “By God, I will have one of his three Is more beloved to me than to have what the sun rises on, to have him say to me what he said to him when he brought him back from Tabuk. Aren’t you pleased to be of me? In the same position as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me. I would rather have what the sun rose upon me, and for him to say to me what he said about me. On the Day of Khaybar: I will give the standard to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. God will grant victory at his hands. He will not flee. He is more beloved to me. Rather than having what the sun rises upon, and being his son-in-law over his daughter, having from her a child that is his, is more beloved to me than having The sun did not rise on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8193","8241 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill, and Fatima came and mourned for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he made her happy, and she cried.” Then she leaned on him, and he made her happy, and she laughed. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I asked her, and she said: Why did you lean on him? He told me that he had died from this pain, so I cried, then fell on him, and he told me that I was rushing my family to catch him, and that I “The mistress of the women of the people of Paradise, except Maryam bint Imran, so I raised my head and laughed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8194","8242 Hilal bin Bishr told me, he said: Muhammad bin Khalid told us, he said: Musa bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Hashim bin Hashim told me On the authority of Abdullah bin Wahb, that Umm Salamah told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Fatima and he spoke to her, and she cried.” Then he spoke to her and she laughed. Umm Salamah said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I asked her about her crying and her laughter. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that he was dying, and I cried. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that I am a lady. The women of the people of Paradise after Maryam bint Imran, so I laughed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8195","8243 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and Fatima is the master of the women of the people of Paradise, except It was not from Maryam, the daughter of Imran.”"
"8196","8244 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Zubayri told us Muhammad bin Abdullah, he said: Abu Ja`far, whose name is Muhammad bin Marwan, who said: Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delayed a day on our behalf until the day had come, so when It was the evening. Someone said to him: O Messenger of God, it has been difficult for us. We did not see you today. He said: An angel from heaven did not see me, so he asked for permission. God visited me, and he told me or gave me good news that my daughter Fatima is the leader of the women of my nation, and that Hasan and Hussein are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8197","8245 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, On the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Fatima came as if her walk was the walk of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Welcome.” With my daughter, then he made her sit on his right or on his left, then he spoke to her and she cried, so I said to her: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, with his speech, and did you cry? Then he confided a speech to her, and she laughed, so I said to her: I have never seen joy closer than today. He was sad, and I asked her about what he said, and she said: I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until when he was arrested I would ask her, and she said: He confided in me, saying: Gabriel used to examine me with the Qur’an once every year, and he examined it with me twice a year, and I do not see it unless I see it. He has come for me, and you are the first of my family to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am to you. She said: So I cried because of that. Then he said: Are you not satisfied with being The mistress of the women of this nation or the women of the believers? She said: I laughed."
"8198","8246 Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq He said: Aisha told me, she said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of us, not one of us left, so Fatima came She was walking, and no, by God, her walk followed the walk of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until she came to him, and he said: Welcome, my daughter. So he made her sit on his right or on his left, then he made her walk with something and she cried intensely, then he made her walk with something and she laughed, so when he got up The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said to her: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, singled you out among us for secrets, and you are crying, tell me. What did he tell you? She said: I would not reveal his secret to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he died, I said to her: I ask you about what I have over you. The truth is, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, please you with? She said: As for now, yes, he pleased me, as for his first time. He said: Gabriel. He used to talk to me about the Qur’an once every year, and he used to talk to me about it twice a year, and I only see that the time has approached, so fear God and be patient, then He said: O Fatima, are you not satisfied with being the mistress of the women of this nation, or the mistress of the women of the worlds? So I laughed? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8199","8247 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on the pulpit, said: “Bani Hisham bin Al-Mughirah asked my permission to marry their daughter to Ali.” Ibn Abi Talib, so I do not give permission, and then I do not give permission unless Ibn Abi Talib wants to divorce my daughter and marry their daughter, for it is only a few Of me, he makes me suspicious of what he likes, and hurts me what hurts her.”"
"8200","8248 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, He said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, saying: I heard Maswar bin Makhramah, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca giving a sermon. Then he said: “The Banu Hisham have asked me for permission to marry their daughter to Ali, but I do not give permission. I do not give permission unless Ibn Abi Talib wants to.” That he separates from my daughter, and that he marries their daughter, and then says: Fatima is a lump or a piece of my semen. What he hurts me hurts me, and he makes me suspicious of what he did. He took her interest, and it was not for him to bring together the daughter of the enemy of God and the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8201","8249 Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us, as I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fatima is an enemy of mine. Whoever makes her angry makes me angry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8202","8250 Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ali bin Shuaib told me Hussein, that Al-Miswar bin Makhramah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fatima is an object of mine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8203","8251 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told me, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halahla, that he narrated to him that Ibn Shihab, narrated to him that Ali bin Hussein narrated to him, that Al-Maswar bin Makhrama, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon on this pulpit, and I was a wet dream on that day. He said: “Fatima is a bitch from me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8204","8252 Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told us, saying: Muhammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Muhammad bin Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for you, O Ali, circumcise me. “And the father of my two sons, and you are of me, and I am of you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8205","8253 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told me, he said: Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Musa, who is the son of Ya’qub al-Zam’i, told me on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Zaid bin Al-Muhajir, he said: Muslim bin Abi Sahl Al-Nabal told me, he said: Hassan bin Osama told me Ibn Zayd Ibn Haritha, he said: Usama Ibn Zayd told me, he said: “I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night for some need. So he came out and was carrying something that I did not know what it was, so when I finished my need, I said: What is this that you are carrying? So he revealed it, and behold He is Al-Hasan, with Al-Hussein on his hips. He said: These are my sons and my daughter’s sons. Oh God, you know that I love them, so I love them. Oh God, you know that I love them, so I love them.”"
"8206","8254 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Yazid bin Mardanbeh told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Yes, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"
"8207","8255 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Naam, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8208","8256 Ahmad bin Harb told us, saying: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Hassan and Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8209","8257 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Adam informed us, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, except The two cousins: Issa, son of Mary, and Yahya, son of Zakaria.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8210","8258 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of some of the companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: meaning Anas bin Malik. He said: “We entered.” And perhaps he said: “I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein turn on his stomach. He said: And he says: My rayhani is from this nation. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8211","8259 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, that his father told him, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, he said: I was with Ibn Umar, and a man came to him and asked him about the blood of a mosquito on his clothes, should he pray? With it? Ibn Omar said: Who are you from? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Who will excuse me from this? He asks me about the blood of mosquitoes, when they killed the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “They are my fragrance from this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8212","8260 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibn Abi Omar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, On the authority of a man who said: I heard Ali, on the pulpit in Kufa, saying: I proposed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Fatima, and he married me. So I said: “O Messenger of God, am I more beloved to you or her?” He said: “She is more beloved to me than you, and you are dearer to me than her.”"
"8213","8261 Abdul-A’la bin Wasil bin Abdul-A’la told us, he said: Ali bin Thabit told us, he said: Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad told us, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali, he said: “I fell ill and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited me May God bless him and grant him peace, so he entered upon me while I was lying down, so he leaned next to me, then he surrounded me with his garment, and when he saw that I had been guided, he went to the mosque. He was praying, and when he finished his prayer, he came and lifted the garment from me, and said: Get up, O Ali, for you have been healed. So I got up as if I had never done anything wrong before that. He said: I have not asked my Lord for anything in my prayer except that He has given it to me, and I have not asked anything for myself except that I have asked of you.” Ja’far al-Ahmar disagreed with him, and said: About Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali"
"8214","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Ja’far Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, said: “I was in severe pain, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he made me stay in his place, and he stood up to pray. He threw a hem of his garment over me, then said: Get up, O Ali, you have been healed. There is no harm in doing so, and I have not prayed for anything for myself except that I have prayed for you the same. And I have not prayed for anything except that it has been answered, or he said: I have been given, except that it has been said to me: There is no prophet after you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8215","8263 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim, who is Ibn Yazid, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya Ibn Ka’b Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: Your uncle, the misguided old man, has died, so who will cover him?” He said: Go and see your father, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I did, then I came to him, and he ordered me to wash, so I washed, and he prayed for me. “Nothing on earth pleases me with any of them.”"
"8216","8264 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Fudayl Abu Muadh told me, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ali, he said: “When I returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said to me a word that I would not like to have in this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8217","8265 Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Hashim ibn Mukhlid al-Thaqafi informed us, saying: My uncle Ayyub ibn Ibrahim, Muhammad ibn Yahya, who is my grandfather, said, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Sayegh, on the authority of Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that Ali “came out to us in extreme heat, wearing winter clothes, and he came out to us in the winter, wearing summer clothes, then he called for water and drank.” Then he wiped the sweat from his forehead, and when he returned to his father, he said: O father, did you see what the Commander of the Faithful did when he came out to us in the winter? He was wearing summer clothes, and he came out to us in the summer, and he was wearing winter clothes. Abu Laila said: Did you understand? He took his son Abd al-Rahman by the hand. So he came to Ali, and Ali said to him: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent to me, and I had severe ophthalmia, so he spit in my eye, then said: Open Your eyes, so I opened them, and I did not complain about them until that time, and he prayed for me and said: Oh God, remove the heat and cold from him, for I did not find any heat, nor \cold until this day of mine.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8218","8266 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili informed us, saying: Qasim Al-Jarmi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman, who is the son of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ali bin Alqamah, on the authority of Ali, said: “When it was revealed: O you who have believed, when you speak to the Messenger, present between I will give you charity. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: Tell them to give in charity. He said: How much, O Messenger of God? He said: In a dinar. He said: They cannot bear it. He said: Half a dinar. He said: They cannot bear it. He said: How much? He said: With a ritual. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You are. To Zuhayd, he said: Then God Almighty revealed: Have you feared that your disputes should be presented before My hands, until the end of the verse, and Ali was saying: By Me, lighten \about this nation\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8219","8267 Muhammad bin Wahb bin Abdullah bin Samak bin Abi Karimah Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Tell us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Muhammad bin Khathim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khathim, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasir, he said: “Ali bin Abi Talib and I were companions in the tribe’s campaign, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, camped there and stayed there, we saw Some people from Bani Mudlij were working in a spring of theirs, or in a palm tree, and Ali said to me: O Abu Al-Yaqzan, would you like us to bring these people? So let us see how they work. He said: I said: If you wish, we can come to them, and we looked at their work for an hour, then we fell asleep, so Ali and I set off to sleep. We slept in the shade of trees of palm trees and lumps of dirt. We slept, and by God, no one alerted us except the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to move us. With his leg, and we had fallen asleep from that deep place in which we slept. On that day, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: What is the matter with you, O Is there dirt? When he saw the dirt on him, then he said: Shall I not tell you about the most miserable of people? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Uhaymar Thamud who? He hamstrung the she-camel, and who will strike you, O Ali, for this? And he put his hand on his horn to make this one wet from it, and took hold of his beard.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8220","8268 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, she said: Umm Salamah said: “Indeed, the most recent of people “A covenant with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Ali.”"
"8221","8269 Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, she said: Umm Salamah said, “And the one by whom she swears Umm Salamah, “If the person closest to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali,” she said: It was not the day after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested. And peace be upon him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for him, and I thought he had sent him for some need, so he started saying: Did Ali come three times? She said: He came before sunrise, and when he came we knew that he had a need for him, so we left the house, and we had visited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. That day, peace be upon him, in Aisha’s house, I was the last one to leave the house, then I sat near the door, and Ali leaned on him. So he was the last of the people to make contact with him, and he made his way and spoke to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8222","8270 Ishaq ibn Ibrahim and Muhammad ibn Qudamah informed us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja’ On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: “We were sitting and waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came out to us, and a vast He put on his sandals, then threw them to Ali, and said: Indeed, there are those among you who fight over the interpretation of the Qur’an, just as I fought over its revelation. Abu Bakr said: He said: No. Omar said: I. He said: No, but the owner of the sandal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8223","8271 Yusuf bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahb, He said: Ali said in Al-Rahba: “I adjure by God the one who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Ghadir Khumm, saying: God is my protector, and I am He is the guardian of the believers, and whoever I am his guardian, then this is his guardian. O God, protect whoever supports him, antagonize whoever antagonizes him, and help whomever helps him.” Saeed said: Six stood beside me, and Haritha bin Mudharib said: Six stood up with me, and Zayd bin Yatha’ said: Six stood up with me, and Amr Dhu Marr said: “ Love the one who loves him, and hate the one who hates him"
"8224","8272 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Khalid narrating , on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ammar: “The group will kill him.” Al-Baghiyya,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Dawud disagreed with him, and said: On the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Al-Hasan (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8225","8273 Amr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ayoub and Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan On the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ammar: “The transgressing group will kill you,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: It was narrated by Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan"
"8226","8274 Humayd ibn Masada informed us, on the authority of Yazid, he is the son of Zuray’. He said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “When it was the Day of the Trench, while he was giving them milk, and the hair on his chest was covered with dust, she said: By God, I have not forgotten him, and he is He says: O God, the good is only the best of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar, and Al-Muhajirah, she said: Ammar came and said: Ibn Sumayyah, this group will kill you. \the transgressor\"""""
"8227","8275 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Umm Al-Hasan said, The Mother of the Believers, Umm Salamah, said: “I have not forgotten the day of the ditch, when he was giving them milk, and his hair was covered with dust, and he was saying: Oh God, it is good.” The best of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar, the Emigrants, and the Emigrants. Ammar came and said: O Ibn Sumayyah, the transgressing group will kill you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8228","8276 Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam and Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ammar: “The group will kill you.” \the transgressor\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8229","8277 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadhar bin Shumayl told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Maslamah, on the authority of Abu Nadra, On the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: Someone better than me, Abu Qatada, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ammar: “Wretched.” “For you, O Ibn Sumayyah, and he wiped the dust from his head, the transgressing group will kill you.”"
"8230","8278 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zaid told us, he said: The common people informed us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Masoud, on the authority of Hanzalah bin خُوَيْلِدٍ ، قَالَ : كُنْتُ عِنْدَ مُعَاوِيَةَ ، فَأَتَاهُ رَجُلانِ يَخْتَصِمَانِ فِي رَأْسِ عَمَّارٍ ، يَقُولُ كُلُّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا أَنَا قَتَلْتُهُ ، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ Allah bin Amr: “Let one of you grant peace to his friend, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The group will kill him.” Al-Baghiyya,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shu’bah disagreed with him, and he said: On the authority of the common people, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Suwayd."
"8231","8279 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of a man from Bani Shayban, on the authority of Hanzala bin Suwayd, said: Ammar’s head was brought, and Abdullah bin Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “The oppressive group will kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8232","8280 Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Ammar is killed by the transgressing group.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Muawiyah disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, Abdullah bin Muhammad informed us, he said: He told us Abu Muawiyah, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, Abdullah bin Amr said, Sufyan Al-Thawri disagreed with something similar, and said: On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Ziyad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8233","8281 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Ziyad, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: I am captives of Abdullah bin Amr, Amr bin Al-Aas, and Muawiyah. Abdullah bin Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The transgressing group will kill Ammar.” Amr said to Muawiyah: Do you hear what this person is saying? So he deleted it and said: We killed him? The one who brought it killed him, and you are still refuting it in your urine."
"8234","8282 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A rogue from among the people will pass by, and the first of the two groups will be killed in truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8235","8283 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My nation will be two groups, and a rogue will emerge from among them, and the first of them will kill her in truth.”"
"8236","8284 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Awf told us, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My nation will separate into two groups, and a rogue will pass between them. The leader of the two groups will kill them justly.”"
"8237","8285 Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Ghaylani informed us, saying: Bahz told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who is Ibn Al-Fadl, he said: Tell us Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A rogue woman passes by a group of people, and you will kill her first.” \The two sects in truth\"""""
"8238","8286 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id On the authority of the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He mentioned people among his nation who would go out in a group of people, with soaring marks on them, abandoning religion.” Just as an arrow passes from the target, they are among the worst of creation, or they are the worst of creation. The closest of the two groups to the truth will kill them. He said: And Amr said: Another word I said between him and me: What is it? He said: You killed them, O people of Iraq. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8239","8287 Abd al-A’la ibn Wasil ibn Abd al-A’la informed us, saying: Muhadhar ibn al-Mu’ri’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Ajlah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, He heard Al-Dahhak Al-Mashriqi speaking to them, and with them were Sa’id bin Jubayr, Maymun bin Abi Shabib, Abu Al-Bakhtari, and Abu Salih. Dhar Al-Hamdani and Al-Hasan Al-Arni narrated that he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri narrating on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “In a people They will leave this nation, so mention their prayers, their zakat, and their fasting. They will leave Islam, just as an arrow leaves its target. No. The Qur’an will go beyond their throats, they will go out in a group of people, and the people closest to the truth will fight them.”"
"8240","8288 Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a recitation by him while I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, He said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: “Between We are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is swearing an oath. Dhu al-Khuwaysaira, a man from Banu Tamim, came to him and said: Oh Messenger of God, be just. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who will be just if I do not be just? I will be defeated and lost if I do not be just. Omar said. “Give me permission to behead him.” He said, “Leave him, for he has companions. One of you deems his prayers to be in contempt with theirs, and his fasting to be with theirs.” They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They shoot from Islam like an arrow shoots from the target, looking at its blade, but nothing is found in it. Then He looks at its surface, but nothing is found on it. Then he looks at its freshness, but nothing is found on it, which is the mug. Then he looks at its dirt. There is nothing in it, anything other than faeces and blood. They are a black man, one of his upper arms is like a woman’s breast, or like a few They went out with the best group of people. Abu Sa`id said: I bear witness that I heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I bear witness that Ali bin Abi Talib fought them, and I was with him. So he ordered that man to go in search and he was found, so he was brought until I looked at him. On the description of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which he described.”"
"8241","9289 Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa ibn Bahlul informed us, saying: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, and he mentioned Another, they said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: “While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, One day, God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore an oath, and Dhu al-Khuwaysarah al-Tamimi said: O Messenger of God, be just. He said: Woe to you, and who can be just? If I do not do justice, Omar stood up and said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to behead him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: No. Indeed, he has companions whose prayers he despises with his prayers, and his fasting with his fasting. He looks at his blade and does not find anything in it. Then he looks at his blade and does not find anything in it. Then he looks at his face and does not find anything in it. There is something in it, then he looks at its filth and does not find anything in it. Previously, excrement and blood. They go out with the best group of people. Oh, they are a man. I call, one of his hands is like a woman’s breast, or like a piece of tea rolling around.” Abu Sa’id said: I bear witness that I heard this from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I bear witness that I was with Ali bin Abi Talib when he fought them, so he was sent to the dead, and he was brought according to the description that was given. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8242","8290 Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, that when Al-Hurriyah went out with Ali bin Abi Talib, they said, “No.” Judgment belongs only to God. Ali said: “A word of truth by which I mean falsehood.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, described people. Indeed, I know their description in These are the ones who speak the truth with their tongues. This is not permissible among them, and he pointed to his throat of one of the most hated of God’s creation to him. Among them are black. One of his hands was a lamb or a teat.” When Ali fought them, he said: Look. They looked, but they did not find anything, so he said: Go back, for God’s sake. I lied, and I did not lie, two or three times, then they found him in ruins, so they brought him and placed him in his hands.” Ubaid Allah said: I am present. That is part of their affair, and Ali’s statement concerning them"
"8243","8291 Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Yazid informed us, saying: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghaflah, He said: I heard Ali saying: “If I tell you about myself, then war is a deception, and if I tell you about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Because something lower than heaven is more beloved to me than lying to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “There will emerge a people who are young in their teeth, foolish in their dreams, who will speak the best speech of the people, whose faith will not go beyond their throats, and they will go forth. from religion as an arrow passes from its target, so if you overtake them, kill them, for for killing them there will be a reward for whoever killed them on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8244","Ahmad bin Sulaiman and Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Suwaid bin He neglected, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A people will emerge from the end of time, reciting the Qur’an, but it will not go beyond their throats.” They will pass from the religion as an arrow passes from its target. Fighting them is a duty upon every Muslim.” Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq disagreed with him, so he entered between Abi Ishaq. And between Suwayd bin Ghaflah and Abd al-Rahman bin Tharwan"
"8245","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Qays al-Awdi, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “At the end of time, a people will emerge They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass away from religion as an arrow passes from its target. Fighting them is a duty upon every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8246","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Ziyad, he said: “We went out with Ali to the Kharijites, and he killed them, then he said: Look, for the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, there will emerge a people who speak the truth, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will emerge from the truth as an arrow emerges from a target. Their marking is: Indeed, among them A black man with scars on his hand, with black hairs on his hand. If it was him, you have killed the worst of people, and if it was not him, then you have killed the best of people. So we cried, then he said: “Seek,” so we sought, and we found the place to come, so we fell down in prostration, and Ali fell down with us, prostrating, except that he said: They speak the word of truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8247","Al-Hasan bin Mudrak told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, he said: Abu Balaj told us Yahya bin Sulaym bin Balj said: Abu Sulaym bin Balj told me that he was with Ali in Nahrawan. He said: “Before that, I was a man There was something on his hand, so I said: What is the matter with your hand? He said: It was eaten by a camel. When it was the day of Nahrawan, and Ali killed Al-Hurriyah, Ali was dismayed by He killed them when he did not find that breast, so he walked around until he found it in a watering can, and said: God has spoken the truth, and he conveyed the message to His Messenger, and he said: On his shoulders were three “Hairs like a nipple.”"
"8248","8296 Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I was While Ali was sitting, a man wearing traveling clothes entered and said: And Ali is speaking to the people, and they are speaking to him, so he said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you call for the call to prayer? Should I speak? He did not pay attention to him, and he was preoccupied with what he was doing, so I sat next to the man and asked him: What happened to you? He said: I was performing Umrah, and I met Aisha, and she said to me: These people who went out in your land are called Hurriyah. I said: They went out in a place He is called Harawra, and they were called that. She said: Blessed is he who witnesses their destruction. If Ibn Abi Talib had wished, he would have informed you of their news. He said: So I came to ask him about their news, and when Ali finished, he said: Where is the one who asks for permission? So he told the story to him as he told it to us. He said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and no one was with him except Aisha, the Mother of the Believers. So he said Me: How are you, Ali, and the people of so-and-so? I said: God and His Messenger know best, and he said: Then he gestured with his hand and said: A people who will come out of the East and recite the Qur’an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass away from religion as an arrow passes from its target. Among them is a man with pain as if his hand was a breast. I adjure you by God, have I told you about them? They said: Yes, he said: I appeal to you by God, did I tell you that he is among them? They said: Yes, he said: Then you came to me and told me that he was not among them, so I swore to you by God that he was among them, so you brought him to me, treating him as he was. I called you? They said: Yes. He said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth."
"8249","8297 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, who is Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: On the day of Nahrawan, he met the Kharijites, and they did not leave until they attacked each other with spears, and they killed them all. Ali said: “ They searched for the mammal. They searched for him but did not find him. Then Ali said: I did not lie, nor did I lie. They searched for him. They searched for him and found him in a clearing. On the ground there were people of the dead, and then there was a man with on his hand what were like the feces of felines. Then Ali and the people said “Allahu Akbar” and the people said “Allahu Akbar” and they liked that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8250","8298 Abd al-A’la ibn Wasil ibn Abd al-A’la informed us, saying: Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, on the authority of Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, said: Ali addressed us at the bridge of Al-Dizjan, and he said: “Indeed, it was mentioned to me about something coming out of Before the east, and among them was a mammal, so he fought them, and the Hurriyah said to one another: Do not speak to him, lest he reject you as he rejected you on the day Harroura, and some of them attacked each other with spears, and a man from Ali’s companions said: Cut the tents, and the tents: the spears, so they turned and turned. Twelve or thirteen men of Ali’s companions were killed, so Ali said: Seek al-Mukhdraj, and that was on the day of Shat, so they said : What we are capable of, so Ali rode the mule of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to a valley from the ground, and said: Search for him among these. So he was brought out and said: I did not lie, nor did I lie. So he said: Work and do not rely. If I had not feared that you would rely, I would have informed you of what was decided. May God bless you with his tongue, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We witnessed people in Yemen, and they said: How, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: It was “Their desire is with us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
